# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env.local` (or `.env`) and fill in. Never commit the filled file.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.example` itself is committed; `.gitignore` ignores `.env*` but makes an
# exception for this file.
#
# There are two kinds of value in here.
#
# 1. Values you COPY from somewhere. If you cannot find one, it is in a
#    dashboard:
#
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID  sanity.io/manage -> your project -> API
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET     sanity.io/manage -> your project -> Datasets
#      RESEND_API_KEY                 resend.com -> API Keys
#      BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN          Vercel -> Storage -> your Blob store
#
# 2. Values that DO NOT EXIST until you create them. Nothing will ever show
#    them to you, and there is nothing to look up. You make them up, save them
#    somewhere safe (a password manager), and paste the same value into Vercel:
#
#      ADMIN_API_KEY                  openssl rand -hex 32
#      CONSENT_LOG_HMAC_SECRET        openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Note that Vercel treats these as secrets: once saved, it never shows the value
# again, only the name. Your own copy is the only copy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Sanity (required) ------------------------------------------------------
# Content API for the project/newsfeed documents. Both values are exposed to the
# browser, so they are configuration rather than secrets. Find them at
# https://sanity.io/manage -> your project -> API.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=""

# --- Resend (required) ------------------------------------------------------
# Sends the contact form submissions from POST /api/contact. SECRET.
RESEND_API_KEY=""

# --- Admin API (required) ---------------------------------------------------
# Guards the internal consent-audit endpoints: GET/DELETE /api/consent-log and
# /api/gdpr/manage. Send it as either header:
#     Authorization: Bearer <key>
#     x-admin-key: <key>
# A `?key=` query parameter is deliberately rejected - it leaks the secret into
# request logs. An unset value disables both endpoints (HTTP 500, fail closed).
# SECRET.
#
# You invent this value; nothing issues it. Generate one and keep it somewhere
# you can retrieve it, e.g. a password manager:
#     openssl rand -hex 32
ADMIN_API_KEY=""

# --- Consent audit log (required in production) -----------------------------
# HMAC key for the tamper-evident consent-log hash chain. SECRET.
#
# You invent this value too - there is no service to copy it from:
#     openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Vercel will not show it back to you once saved (dashboard Secret variables and
# `vercel env pull` are write-only), so store it in a password manager the moment
# you create it. If you lose it you cannot recover it, only replace it.
#
# Replacing it is not free: existing entries were signed with the old key, so those
# signatures can never be checked again. The hash chain itself
# (previousHash -> currentHash) is unaffected, and still catches an entry whose
# content or links were rewritten.
#
# When you rotate, move SIGNATURES_VALID_FROM in lib/consent-logger.ts forward to
# the moment of the rotation: entries before it are then reported as "predate the
# signing key" instead of as failures. The key was rotated once already, on
# 2026-09-29; see docs/HANDOVER-CLEANUP.md for what that cost.
#
# If this is unset, lib/consent-logger.ts logs a `console.warn` per consent
# submission and stores an empty signature, and verification skips the signature
# check entirely: the log still chains, but nothing proves it was not rewritten.
# It defends against someone holding the Blob token without this key; it does not
# defend against a compromised app.
CONSENT_LOG_HMAC_SECRET=""

# --- Vercel Blob (required) -------------------------------------------------
# The consent audit log is stored as the private blob `consent-audit.log`, not
# on the local filesystem (Vercel's filesystem is ephemeral and read-only
# outside /tmp). Vercel injects this token automatically in deployments; for
# local development create a Blob store and copy its read/write token here.
# SECRET.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""
